# Redmine's Mercurial adapter assembled the hg command line from
# request-derived values passed as standalone arguments next to their option
# flags (CWE-88, argument injection). Mercurial's early option parser rescans
# the whole command line for its own global options -- --config, --repo,
# --debugger -- even where a subcommand has begun, so a standalone
# --config=alias.rhdiff=!xterm anywhere in the argv turns one hg invocation
# into arbitrary command execution. The values arrive from the repository
# browser routes (path, identifier, branch, limit) and reach hg untouched by
# the per-element shell quoting, which escapes shell metacharacters but
# leaves a leading -- intact:
#
#   hg 'rhcat', '-r', CGI.escape(hgrev(identifier)), '--', hgtarget(p)
#
# Ticket #27516 landed as three commits in the same minute. The pool row
# names the last of them, 9d797400, which glues each value to its flag
# ("-r#{value}", "--limit=#{value}") so the value can never stand alone and be
# rescanned as an option; its parent carries the first commit's
# blocklist (ca87bf76, "reject malicious command argument"), which is the
# half NVD's text describes ("does not block the --config and --debugger
# flags"), and the second's -- separators. Nothing detects any revision:
#
#   - VYQL-INJ-031, the argument-injection rule, has no Ruby emitter at all
#     (the 1050/1085/1086 ENGINE-GAPS family).
#   - The CWE-78 fallback VYQL-INJ-002 is structurally dead for this assembly
#     pattern in Ruby: processArgVectorApplicator (bindings_apply.go:1317)
#     stamps core.ProcessArgVector, which neutralizes
#     injection.CommandInjection, on any array literal whose first element is
#     a literal, with no check that the sequence reaches a process as an argv
#     vector. Redmine joins the array into one shell string for IO.popen and
#     still gets the safe-argv credit. Minimal pair, both unescaped params ->
#     IO.popen(string): ['rhcat', '-r', rev].join(' ') reports 0, while the
#     identical code with the first element a variable reports CRITICAL
#     VYQL-INJ-002.
#   - Ruby does not resolve a call into a splat-parameter method:
#     hg(*args, &block) is "callee not traced -- external or cross-package",
#     so taint dies at the adapter boundary even where a source exists.
#   - The remediation cuts no flow. The fixed "-r#{value}" carries the same
#     params -> IO.popen path as the vulnerable '-r', value (both measured
#     reaching the sink on an inlined pair), and the only difference is the
#     lexical adjacency of flag and value inside one argv element. The Ruby
#     binding feature set (callPath, functionName, literal, paramName, field,
#     attr, assign, selector, expr) has no call-argument tokens, so adjacency
#     is not stateable; keying on hg, hg_args or shellout would encode this
#     fixed revision's own layout. The blocklist variant of the change has the same
#     problem in the other direction: the guard is a private regex inside
#     the callee, visible only as its own constant names.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-analysis-gap

test "rank1664: a request-derived revision reaches hg as a standalone argument after its flag"
  lang ruby
  file lib/redmine/scm/adapters/mercurial_adapter.rb
  reject VYQL-INJ-031
  code
  ```
  module Redmine
    module Scm
      module Adapters
        class MercurialAdapter
          def cat(path, identifier = nil)
            rev = params[:rev]
            hg 'rhcat', '-r', rev, '--', path do |io|
              io.binmode
              io.read
            end
          end

          def hg(*args, &block)
            full_args = ['-R', root_url, '--encoding', 'utf-8']
            full_args += args
            shellout(
              self.class.sq_bin + ' ' + full_args.map { |e| shell_quote e.to_s }.join(' '),
              &block
            )
          end

          def shellout(cmd, &block)
            IO.popen(cmd, 'r+') { |io| block.call(io) }
          end

          def root_url
            '/var/repos/project'
          end

          def params
            {}
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1664: the fixed revision glues the value into the flag's own argument"
  lang ruby
  file lib/redmine/scm/adapters/mercurial_adapter.rb
  reject VYQL-INJ-031
  code
  ```
  module Redmine
    module Scm
      module Adapters
        class MercurialAdapter
          def cat(path, identifier = nil)
            rev = params[:rev]
            hg 'rhcat', "-r#{rev}", '--', path do |io|
              io.binmode
              io.read
            end
          end

          def hg(*args, &block)
            full_args = ["-R#{root_url}", '--encoding=utf-8']
            full_args += args
            shellout(
              self.class.sq_bin + ' ' + full_args.map { |e| shell_quote e.to_s }.join(' '),
              &block
            )
          end

          def shellout(cmd, &block)
            IO.popen(cmd, 'r+') { |io| block.call(io) }
          end

          def root_url
            '/var/repos/project'
          end

          def params
            {}
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```
